  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...A series of small \ndisturbances and onshore flow will bring steady rain to the \nregion through the end of the week. A weak surface high building \nover the southeastern Gulf will reinforce onshore flow and could \npotentially tighten pressure gradients across the panhandle as the\nnext system approaches. A low pressure system originating near \nRussia will move east, tracking south of the Aleutian Islands and \ninto the Gulf of Alaska by early weekend. There is a growing \nlikelihood of tropical moisture entraining into the system, \nsupported by an 850mb southerly jet, increased precipitable water,\nand seasonably warmer temperatures aloft. Though this will likely\nnot affect the surface much due to consistent widespread cloud \ncover and small diurnal trends.\n\nModel spread is still significant, but guidance favors landfall \nalong the north-central coast late weekend. The system could bring\nrounds of moderate to heavy rain across most of the panhandle, \nwith the highest totals currently expected along the northeast \nGulf coast, though this is dependent on the system's exact track \nand strength. There is also increasing potential for stronger \nwinds and building seas along the outer coast and northern inner \nchannels ahead of this low. While some guidance suggests a more \naggressive evolution, the system generally lacks upper level \nsupport beyond a weak, negatively tilted trough and jet setup. We \nwill continue to monitor developments through the week.",
